{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792203274,"nonce":"xa4WsjsDmMGfrfxPd1S9KlIOmdc=","title":"Structure typedefs pre-registered as a Class placeholder never become aliases","message":"A typedef in a module lowered after its first use is pre-registered as SymbolKind::Class, and type resolution keeps building `Class { symbol, args }` for it after the typedef's body is lowered (the symbol's type is a TypeAlias by then). Its fields are then unknown, and member access types as Dynamic. The Class arm of resolve_type_path already special-cases `Map` for this; other typedefs are not handled.\n\nSeen with haxe.coro.AsyncIterator\u003cInt\u003e as the return type of an abstract's iterator() in TestCoroutines: lowering an AsyncIterable loop first made the abstract's iterator() type as Dynamic. The coroutine pass works around it by reading the declared return type from the signature index.\n\nTried and reverted: resolving a Class-kind symbol whose type is a TypeAlias over an Anonymous target as that alias. It fixed the AsyncIterator case but lost TestMatch, because structural receivers then go through the by-name stdlib class scan in stdlib_runtime.rs (`MiniRef\u003cT\u003e.get()` bound to a stdlib `get`). Fixing this needs that scan narrowed first (see the issue on structural receivers).","files":null}]}